  "lede": "Along the cost frontier, the next point of pass rate costs {price.nano-xs.low.r1.nano-xs.high.r1.pass_rate.monthly_per_point} a month at the cheap end and {price.brisk-s.high.r1.atlas-m.high.r1.pass_rate.monthly_per_point} at the top. Adding a retry to Atlas-M or Brisk-S is the cheapest gain.",
  "recommends": [],
  "flag": "No gate, floor, margin or control was declared, so no option is ruled in or out, and all arms were compared on unpaired overall figures. Costs are at this run's provider routing, which the snapshot does not name.",
  "confidence": {
    "form": "low",
    "caveats": [
      {"id": "nothing_declared", "material_if": "the owner declares a minimum pass rate or a price per point: the lean then changes, and the price bands in the claims set where it does."},
      {"id": "no_control", "material_if": "a claim that one arm beats another is read as a paired result: none is, so a gap between arms with overlapping intervals is not told apart."},
      {"id": "best_of_n", "material_if": "the pick leads its neighbour by little: the best of {n_candidates} candidates reads high by chance, and a re-run on fresh cases would likely read it lower."}
    ]
  },
  "decision": [
    {"slot": "the_trade", "text": "Moving up the frontier from {measure.cost_per_1k.nano-xs.off.r0.mean} per 1k calls to {measure.cost_per_1k.brisk-s.high.r1.mean} lifts pass rate from {measure.pass_rate.nano-xs.off.r0.mean} to {measure.pass_rate.brisk-s.high.r1.mean}. Most of the gain comes early and cheaply."},
